        <p>MEET OF COATS. At Warrington en Monday Frank McCoy, Rose and Crown-street, was charged with stealing from the shop doorway of Benedict Tvrer, Winwick-street, two men's coats, of the value of 103.—Superintendent Monaghan said that Mr. Tyrer's assistant, Walter Bracegirdle, saw the coats safe at the door at six o'clock on Saturday night. At 6.10 they were missing, and from information he received he went down Winwick-street, and near the Bay horse Inn-saw the prisoner carrying the coats ender his arm. He took him back to the shop and sent for the police. P.C. Baxendale arrived and took him into custody. Prisoner, who said he Acas so drunk that he did not know whether he took them or not, was seat to gaol for 14 days.</p>
        <p>COMMERCIAL FAILURES.—According to " Kepi Mercantile Gazette," the total number of commercial. failures recorded in England and Wales during the week ending Friday, December 28th. was 100, VIZ. :—New Bankruptcy Proceedings published in the London- Gszette,.so ; Deeds of Arrangement registered, 50. The respective numbers in the corresponding week of last year were : Bankruptcies, 28 ; Deeds of Arrangement, 45—Total, 73 ; being a decrease of "ri. The total number of commercial failures recorded 152 weeks of of the present year is 8,329. The total number recorded in the corresponding 52 weeks of the past year was 8,913, showing a decrease of 614.</p>
