      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-05_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>FASHION FORECAST.</head>
        <p>A FASHION FORECAST.</p>
        <p>The latest development of the long glove. says the Onlooker, is tho flexible snake bracelet with</p>
        <p>a jewelled head to hold .it firmly at the elbow, or an expanding jewelled chain bracelet. The "slave" bangle is prinefpallY used for the same purpose. but. on dit that before 'long our sleeves —or, at least, our ruffles—will fall well over our knuckles. The -English modistes are - fighting against it—mais nous, verrons. As for the minia- ture gold hairpins for fastening stray curls to the brim of a hat, they are just what we have. been longing for for years, only we did not know it, and • they are selling like wildfire, as the saying goes.</p>
        <p>''• TO-DAY'S RECIPE,</p>
        <p>TURXEY ON TOAST,---For this take the remains (about lib.) of cold turkey, pint of milk or cream, two eggs, some rounds of bread, a small piece of butter, pepper, and, salt to taste. Cut off the meat of the turk6y and chop it very finely. Put the bones and trimmings into a 4tewpan, with enouzh cold water, tokeovcr then.</p>
      </div>
