      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-01-05_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>STEALING A WATCH AT PRF:.-.COT.</head>
        <p>STEALING A WATCH AT PRF:.-.COT.</p>
        <p>At Prescot Sessions, on Tuesday, John Doyle, stranger, was charged with stealing a silver watch from the person. of Mr. William Lloyd, a retired watchmaker, on Monday. Superintendent Baxendale stated that on Monday night about seven o'clock Mr. Lloyd was in the EaglA and Child Hotel, Prescot, when prisoner came into the same room. About eight o'clock they came to the hotel together, and as soon as they got into the street prisoner knocked Mr. Lloyd on the floor and snatched his watch from hih waistcoat pocket, breaking a silver chain attached. On this charge he was com- mitted for trial. The prisoner was further charged with assaulting Police Constable Siney, who arrested him. For this offence prisoner was committed to prison or two months' hard labour.</p>
        <p>A man has been arrested at Chester who is supposed, from a finger-print test, to be John Davies, the ex-convict, who escaped from Hanley police cells a few weeks ago. The Barnsley Coroner on Wednesday told the father of Laura Ford (15),wb0 jumped from a bedroom window through fright at the man's threats of murder, that he was morally responsible for the girls death.</p>
      </div>
