        <p>The Warrington Corporation has declined the cequest of the Board of Agriculture to adopt regula- tions under the Dogs' Act of 1906 requiring digs to wear collars whilst in a highway or public resort. •:t • A complaint from the "gents' outfitters" may be anticipated. Dogs ought to wear collars if their masters do. The tie may be dispensed with, but the collar—our badge of civilization—No ! An amusing incident occurred at the meeting of the Warrington Rural District Council on Wednesday. At the outset the Clerk read a telegram from the Medical Officer, in which he stated that he could not be present as he had missed his train. At a later stage Mr. Ball entered the room, and noting the absence of the Doctor proceeded to make excuses on his behalf. He was warned that the Doctor had telegraphed an'explanation, but, persisting, muck to the delight of his fellow Councillors, said " You kncw. the Doctor is so busy he really could not come."</p>
